What is carried across from Strata, and what is not:

  docs/BENCH_NOISE.md     written on the Strata checkout 2026-10-xx, ours. The measurement floor
                          Shadow holds itself to: 10.1% median, 27.0% p90, 51.9% worst.
  docs/history/SPEED_BRANCH.md ours (Andre and a3k6g). Every number in it was measured on Strata
                          hardware and is quoted as measured there, not re-claimed here.
  docs/history/RUST_HOST.md ours. The decision about where the seam goes.
  docs/history/RUST_ENGINE.md ours. The order the hybrid work was walked in (M1-M8).
  docs/history/RUST_ENGINE_NEXT.md ours. What was left of that.
  docs/SHADOW_PLAN.md     ours. The plan for this project, written 2026-10-25.
  tools/shadow_harness.py ours (was tools/pi_harness.py on the Strata checkout).

Borrowed from Strata, used as is:

  models/mtp-basalt-ft1   the MTP draft head (dense.bin, experts.bin, draft_vocab.bin), trained
                          on the Strata side. Optional: loaded only with `--mtp DIR`. Shadow's
                          loader for it, crates/shadow-cuda/src/mtp.rs, is ours.

From other projects:

  crates/shadow-model/src/quant_tables.rs
                          the IQ quant formats' lookup tables (grids, sign patterns, IQ4_NL
                          values) from ggml (MIT, ggml.ai), generated through the gguf Python
                          package by tools/gen_quant_tables.py. They are the formats' definition.
  crates/shadow-model/src/unicode_table.rs
                          Unicode general categories, generated from Python's unicodedata.
  docs/ARCH.md            written from the GGUF file and from the published reference
                          implementation (Hugging Face transformers, models/qwen4_exp, Apache-2.0)
                          and llama.cpp's conversion/qwen4exp.py (MIT). Read, not copied.

No source code from Strata's engine has been copied into this project; Shadow's engine is
its own. What came across is the plan, the measurements and the harness (all written by us on
a Strata checkout) and the borrowed parts listed above, all MIT for the same reason Strata is.
Shadow borrows from Strata and other projects where it helps, and lists each borrowing here.

The model this is built to run - Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, abliterated, IQ3_S - is not part of
this repository and is not covered by this license.
